${C_HEAD}Usage:${C_OFF} ${C_CMD}waterbox start${C_OFF} [<session> | --here] [--gui|--no-gui|--x11] [--no-gpu]

Boot the box if it isn't already up, then attach to a tmux session inside it. This
is the default command, so a bare '${C_CMD}waterbox${C_OFF}' does exactly the same thing. Sessions
outlive your terminal: ${C_CMD}Ctrl-b d${C_OFF} detaches (it keeps running), '${C_CMD}exit${C_OFF}' ends it.

  ${C_DIM}(no args)${C_OFF}          Open the session picker — Enter attach · a new · r rename ·
                     d kill · q quit. With no live sessions it just asks for a name.
